Branch Deck's patch of @base-ui/react@1.9.0 (patchedDependencies of pnpm-workspace.yaml; docs/contributing/frontend.md,
"Patched Dependencies"). pnpm applies the diffs below and ignores this text.

The bug: every popup part (TooltipPopup, PopoverPopup, MenuPopup, PreviewCardPopup, NavigationMenuList, through
useHoverFloatingInteraction) takes the HoverInteraction its trigger shares (useHoverInteractionSharedState) and
registers its `dispose` as an unmount effect of its own, which clears `restTimeout` and `openChangeTimeout`. A closed
popup unmounts at the end of its exit: the pointer back over the trigger after a close that was not the hover's (its
view hid, a press of an item) had started the open delay, the unmount cleared it, and the popup opened only at the next
move of the pointer.

The fix, in both builds (.mjs and .js): `useHoverInteractionSharedState(store, ownsTimers = true)`, and
useHoverFloatingInteraction passes false: only a trigger clears the timers of its hover as it unmounts.

An upgrade fails loudly: `allowUnusedPatches` and `allowNonAppliedPatches` stay unset (false), so `pnpm install` stops
with "The following patches were not used" once the lockfile has another version of @base-ui/react, and with "error
applying hunk" when a hunk no longer fits. Re-port it onto the new version: the master of Base UI (5aacdbb78,
2026-11-10) keeps the shared state in HoverIntent (packages/react/src/utils/popups/interactions/hoverIntent.ts) and still
calls `intent.cancelPendingOpen()` in the cleanup of the popup's unmount effect (useHoverPopupInteraction.ts:60-66),
while the trigger cancels it on its own unmount (useHoverTriggerInteraction.ts:102-104): drop that call from the popup's
cleanup and keep `intent.restoreOutsidePointerEvents()`. Then `pnpm patch-commit`, this header put back above its
changes (pnpm writes none), `pnpm install`, and the E2E tests of "Hover back over a trigger whose popup closed"
(tests/e2e/branch-row-layout/branch-row-layout.spec.ts) in Chromium and WebKit: they fail without the patch. Drop the
patch once a release leaves the pending open of the trigger to the trigger.

